Here are the assert statements that are provided in the comments.

1. <code>ArrayList size increases by 1 after insertion </code>

Here's the corresponding C# code:

```cs
[PexMethod]
public void PUT_InsertContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x, int index)
{
    AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index <= arrList.Count && index >= 0);

    int Old_arrListSize = arrList.Count;

    arrList.Insert(index, x);

    int New_arrListSize = arrList.Count;

    Assert.That(New_arrListSize, Is.EqualTo(Old_arrListSize + 1));
}
```

2. <code>ArrayList counts are equal after remove </code>

Here's the corresponding C# code:

```cs
[PexMethod]
public void PUT_RemoveContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x)
{
    AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(true);

    int Old_arrListSize = arrList.Count;
    int Old_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);

    arrList.Remove(x);

    int New_arrListSize = arrList.Count;
    int New_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);

    if (Old_arrListIndexOfX < 0 || New_arrListSize == Old_arrListSize) {
        Assert.That(New_arrListSize, Is.EqualTo(Old_arrListSize));
    } 
    else {
        Assert.That(New_arrListSize, Is.EqualTo(Old_arrListSize - 1));
    }
}
```

3. <code>ArrayList does not increase size after insert after remove</code>
