```cs
[PexMethod]
public void PUT_AddContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x) {
    int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    int Old_x = x;
    int Old_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
    int Old_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
    bool Old_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

    int New_Ret = arrList.Add(x);

    int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    int New_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
    int New_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
    bool New_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

    Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListCount + 1, New_arrListCount, "@@@ The size of ArrayList should increase by 1 after addition.");
    Assert.AreEqual(Old_x, New_Ret, "@@@ The method should return the index where the added item was inserted.");
    Assert.AreEqual(Old_x, New_arrListLastIndexOfX, "@@@ LastIndexOf should indicate insertion index after addition.");
    Assert.True(New_arrListContainsX, "@@@ Contains should return true after addition.");
    Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListIndexOfX, New_arrListIndexOfX, "@@@ IndexOf should not change post-addition.");
    Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX, New_arrListLastIndexOfX, "@@@ LastIndexOf should not change post-addition.");
}
``` 

The above code ensures the consistency between different aspects of an ArrayList collection. The 'Add' function adds an item to the list, increasing the size by 1 and returning the index where the item was inserted. 'Contains' returns true if the item exists. 'IndexOf' always returns the index where the item was added, 'LastIndexOf' returns the same index. The code also checks if any of these properties change after addition, which corresponds to the post-condition.  

